"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":7,"created_at":"2025-03-15T15:18:44Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T17:02:33Z","closed_at":"2025-04-15T00:42:56Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n - Reproducible in: v4.4.stable.mono.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable.mono - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6109) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13600KF (20 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen subclassing the AnimationTree class, animations starts excessively generating `StringName`'s. If it isn't subclassed, this does not happen. This excess causes noticable stutters when the memory is reclaimed.\n\nHere's a graph where I don't subclass the AnimationTree\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b344ad6f-963b-4e7e-8703-8ebfe1a72942\n\nHere's a graph where I subclass the AnimationTree\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ef809afa-b9a1-4dd1-ac14-2d624333f341\n\nBoth cases are doing the same updates.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a custom class inheriting from AnimationTree\n2. Give it a method\n3. Have the method update parameters\n\nRepro is attached\n1. Run the project (non-normal)\n2. Profile memory usage\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nBugged (with subclass): [StringNameLeak.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19263124/StringNameLeak.zip)\nNormal (without subclass): [StringNameLeak (normal).zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19263181/StringNameLeak.normal.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"http